{
  "comment1": "Syno_Toolbox module manifest",
  "comment2": "see modules_json_field_reference.md for field meanings",
  "modules": [
    {
      "id": "dsm_version",
      "category": "info",
      "name": "DSM Version",
      "control": "toggle-display",
      "script": "bin/modules/dsm_version.sh",
      "trigger": "boot",
      "live": true,
      "run_args": [],
      "disable_args": null,
      "check_args": []
    },
    {
      "id": "eth_speed",
      "category": "info",
      "name": "LAN port connected speed",
      "control": "toggle-display",
      "script": "bin/modules/eth_speed.sh",
      "trigger": "boot",
      "live": true,
      "run_args": [],
      "disable_args": null,
      "check_args": []
    },
    {
      "id": "network_mac",
      "category": "info",
      "name": "LAN port MAC address",
      "control": "toggle-display",
      "script": "bin/modules/network_mac.sh",
      "trigger": "boot",
      "live": true,
      "run_args": [],
      "disable_args": null,
      "check_args": []
    },
    {
      "id": "wol_status",
      "category": "info",
      "name": "LAN port WOL status",
      "control": "toggle-display",
      "script": "bin/modules/wol_status.sh",
      "trigger": "boot",
      "live": true,
      "run_args": [],
      "disable_args": null,
      "check_args": []
    },
    {
      "id": "ups_connected",
      "category": "info",
      "name": "UPS Status",
      "control": "toggle-display",
      "script": "bin/modules/ups_status.sh",
      "trigger": "boot",
      "live": true,
      "run_args": [],
      "disable_args": null,
      "check_args": [],
      "result_style": "monospace"
    },
    {
      "id": "system_partition_info",
      "category": "info",
      "name": "DSM System Partition Information",
      "control": "toggle-display",
      "script": "bin/modules/system_partition_info.sh",
      "trigger": "boot",
      "live": true,
      "run_args": [],
      "disable_args": null,
      "check_args": [],
      "note": "candidate for header display instead of a toggle row"
    },
    {
      "id": "var_log_size",
      "category": "info",
      "name": "DSM temp logs size",
      "control": "toggle-display",
      "script": "bin/modules/var_log_size.sh",
      "trigger": "boot",
      "live": true,
      "run_args": [],
      "disable_args": null,
      "check_args": []
    },
    {
      "id": "created_date",
      "category": "info",
      "name": "Synology Created Date",
      "control": "toggle-display",
      "script": "bin/modules/syno_created_date.sh",
      "trigger": "boot",
      "live": true,
      "run_args": [],
      "disable_args": null,
      "check_args": [],
      "note": "candidate for header display instead of a toggle row"
    },
    {
      "id": "telnet_password",
      "category": "info",
      "name": "DSM Telnet Password of the Day",
      "control": "toggle-display",
      "script": "bin/modules/dsm_telnet_password.sh",
      "trigger": "boot",
      "live": true,
      "run_args": [],
      "disable_args": null,
      "check_args": [],
      "result_style": "monospace"
    },
    {
      "id": "send_wol",
      "category": "tools",
      "name": "Send WOL",
      "control": "toggle-wol-selector",
      "script": "bin/modules/send_wol.sh",
      "trigger": "on_save",
      "live": false,
      "run_args": ["{mac}"],
      "disable_args": null,
      "check_args": null,
      "note": "No real 'enabled' state - this is a one-shot action fired by its own Send button, not by Save's enable-diff or boot. trigger stays on_save purely so run_boot_modules.sh never auto-fires it; the toggle checkbox is hidden in the UI and never flips, so that diff path never actually runs. run_args' {mac} placeholder is filled from current_fields.mac, which the Send button persists via save() immediately before calling run - same placeholder-from-saved-conf-field mechanism as seq_io's {volumes}/{kb}, just never previously exercised via a manual button click. NEEDS DAVE'S CONFIRMATION: (1) that synotoolbox_api.sh's run_module_script() resolver re-reads {mac} from conf's send_wol_mac key at run time, the same way it presumably does for seq_io's {volumes}/{kb} - that path has only ever been exercised via Save's enable-diff before, never via a standalone button click straight after a save, so it's unverified for this flow; (2) requires a new listwoldevices action added to synotoolbox_api.sh that reads wol_devices.tsv and returns [{mac,ip,host}] - modelled on discovernas' response shape but not yet implemented."
    },
    {
      "id": "fix_size_units",
      "category": "tools",
      "name": "Change Size Units to Binary",
      "control": "toggle-display",
      "script": "bin/modules/syno_fix_size_units.sh",
      "trigger": "boot",
      "live": false,
      "run_args": [],
      "disable_args": ["--disable"],
      "check_args": ["--check"]
    },
    {
      "id": "cleanup_coredumps",
      "category": "tools",
      "name": "Cleanup Coredumps",
      "control": "toggle-display",
      "script": "bin/modules/syno_clean_coredumps.sh",
      "trigger": "boot",
      "live": false,
      "run_args": [],
      "disable_args": null,
      "check_args": ["--check"]
    },
    {
      "id": "low_current_spinup",
      "category": "tools",
      "name": "Enable Seagate Low Current Spinup",
      "control": "toggle-display",
      "script": "bin/modules/seagate_lowcurrentspinup.sh",
      "trigger": "boot",
      "live": false,
      "run_args": [],
      "disable_args": null,
      "check_args": ["check"]
    },
    {
      "id": "uninstall_active_insight",
      "category": "tools",
      "name": "Uninstall Active Insight",
      "control": "toggle-run",
      "script": "bin/modules/uninstall_active_insight.sh",
      "trigger": "boot",
      "live": false,
      "run_args": [],
      "disable_args": null,
      "check_args": ["check"],
      "note": "run_args wraps: sudo /usr/syno/bin/synopkg uninstall ActiveInsight - confirm exact wrapper script contents before shipping"
    },
    {
      "id": "schedule_ups_connected",
      "category": "tools",
      "name": "Check Connected to UPS Server",
      "control": "toggle-schedule",
      "script": "bin/modules/check_ups_connected.sh",
      "trigger": "scheduled",
      "live": false,
      "run_args": [],
      "disable_args": null,
      "check_args": null,
      "schedule": { "default_repeat_hour": 6 }
    },
    {
      "id": "config_backup",
      "category": "tools",
      "name": "DSM Configuration Backup and Export",
      "control": "toggle-config-backup",
      "script": "bin/modules/synology_config_backup.sh",
      "trigger": "scheduled",
      "live": false,
      "run_args": [],
      "disable_args": null,
      "check_args": null,
      "schedule": { "default_repeat_week": 1 },
      "note": "Script reads its own settings straight from toolbox.conf (config_backup_* keys) rather than taking CLI args - run_args stays empty. Conf keys mirror the script's own variable names: target_dir, remote_backup, remote_port, remote_ip, remote_dir, local_user, remote_user, and the same set prefixed remote2_/local2_ for the 2nd optional remote. Discover NAS is repurposed here to prefill Remote IP fields, not as a source-NAS list."
    },
    {
      "id": "synoboot_backup",
      "category": "tools",
      "name": "Backup Synoboot Image",
      "control": "toggle-filepicker",
      "script": "bin/modules/synoboot_backup.sh",
      "trigger": "boot",
      "live": false,
      "run_args": [],
      "disable_args": null,
      "check_args": null,
      "filepicker": { "label": "Backup destination path" }
    },
    {
      "id": "seq_io",
      "category": "tools",
      "name": "Enable Sequential I/O for SSD Cache",
      "control": "toggle-volume-numeric",
      "script": "bin/modules/syno_seq_io.sh",
      "trigger": "boot",
      "live": false,
      "run_args": ["--volumes={volumes}", "--kb={kb}"],
      "disable_args": ["--volumes={volumes}", "--kb=1024"],
      "check_args": ["--check"],
      "numeric": { "label": "Sequential I/O (kb)", "default": 1024, "min": 4 },
      "volume_source": "listvolumes",
      "note": "Confirmed CLI: --volumes=VOLUME[,VOLUME...] --kb=KB. Disable re-runs with --kb=1024 against the same selected volumes."
    },
    {
      "id": "shr_switch",
      "category": "tools",
      "name": "Switch between SHR and RAID Group or Enable RAID F1",
      "control": "toggle-selector",
      "script": "bin/modules/syno_shr_switch.sh",
      "trigger": "on_save",
      "live": false,
      "run_args": ["{mode}", "{raidf1}"],
      "disable_args": null,
      "check_args": ["--check"],
      "selector": {
        "options": [
          { "label": "SHR", "value": "shr" },
          { "label": "RAID Group", "value": "raidgrp" }
        ],
        "secondary_toggle": { "label": "RAID F1", "value": "raidf1" }
      },
      "note": "Confirmed positional CLI: syno_shr_switch.sh <shr|raidgrp> [raidf1]. raidf1 is an optional 2nd positional arg. Our placeholder substitution always passes 2 args - when RAID F1 isn't checked, {raidf1} resolves to an empty string rather than being omitted entirely. ASSUMPTION (not confirmed by Dave): the script treats an empty/non-matching 2nd arg the same as a missing one. Verify against the actual script before relying on this."
    },
    {
      "id": "restore_fan_speed",
      "category": "tools",
      "name": "Restore RS3621 Fan Speed",
      "control": "toggle-display",
      "script": "bin/modules/restore_rs3621_fan_speed.sh",
      "trigger": "boot",
      "live": false,
      "run_args": [],
      "disable_args": null,
      "check_args": ["check"]
    },
    {
      "id": "toggle_reset_button",
      "category": "tools",
      "name": "Disable Reset Button",
      "control": "toggle-display",
      "script": "bin/modules/toggle_reset_button.sh",
      "trigger": "boot",
      "live": false,
      "run_args": ["disable"],
      "disable_args": ["enable"],
      "check_args": ["check"],
      "note": "single script, 3 modes (enable/disable/check) verified by Dave - not separate files"
    }
  ]
}
